# Cerberus system user for the API service. Installed to
# /usr/lib/sysusers.d/cerberus.conf and applied by %sysusers_create_compat in
# the spec's %pre.
#
# Shipping this file is not merely the modern idiom -- it is required. Several
# %files entries carry %attr(...,cerberus,cerberus,...), and rpm's dependency
# generator turns those into `Requires: user(cerberus)` and
# `Requires: group(cerberus)`. A packaged sysusers.d file is the only thing that
# emits the matching Provides, so a hand-rolled useradd in %pre leaves the
# package uninstallable: dnf and rpm alike refuse with "nothing provides
# user(cerberus)". Confirmed on rpm 6.0.2; older rpm (4.16, 4.20) does not
# generate the dependency, which is why this went unnoticed.
#
# The 'u' type creates both the group and the user. The home directory
# (/etc/cerberus) is shipped by the package. Shell is /sbin/nologin here --
# Debian uses /usr/sbin/nologin and Arch /usr/bin/nologin, which is why this
# fragment is per-format rather than shared.
#Type Name     ID GECOS             Home          Shell
u     cerberus -  "Cerberus SSH CA" /etc/cerberus /sbin/nologin
